WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.760
Models should be managed as operational assets,

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.875
not random files that accumulate over time.

00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:09.160
Names and tags help identify what is being used, but they are not a complete inventory.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.720
Teams still need documentation that explains which models are required,

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.090
which are experimental, which are approved for shared use, which are deprecated,

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.460
and which can be removed safely.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.150
Storage planning matters because model files can be large.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.100
A quick experiment may consume meaningful disk space,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.860
and several experiments can fill a workstation or shared server faster than expected.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.280
When storage runs out, model pulls can fail, applications can break,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.500
logs may stop writing,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.735
and operators may waste time figuring out which files are safe to delete.

00:00:34.735 --> 00:00:38.375
Pulling a model for a personal test is different from approving a model for a team

00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:39.060
workflow.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.140
Shared use should include basic review: why the model is needed,

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.320
what hardware it requires, what license or usage expectations apply, who owns it,

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.200
and how it will be updated or retired.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.850
That review does not need to be heavy, but it should be visible.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.860
Good inventory discipline prevents confusion across machines.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.330
Operators should know where models are stored, how much space they consume,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.645
which hosts need which models, and what cleanup routine exists.

00:01:00.645 --> 00:01:04.540
Storage planning turns local AI from a collection of one-off downloads into a manageable

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.320
environment.
